    "narrative": "For the June 2nd slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.31) and **Jackson Merrill** (62.21) emerge as our most reliable offensive anchors. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Bachar, where his platoon advantage translates into a 14% efficiency boost, further elevated by his prime spot in the #2 hole. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a high-ceiling start against Nola; while Nola presents a decent challenge, **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s 13% platoon edge and consistent middle-of-the-order output make him our highest-projected play. **Kyle Tucker** (61.21) remains a must-start despite the neutral platoon against Soroka, as his base efficiency remains the gold standard for our squad, even if we are awaiting official confirmation of his #5 spot in the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed on the bench with a 47.33 score. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the favorable park and a positive platoon adjustment against Early, his overall efficiency profile could not quite overtake the likes of **Miguel Vargas** (57.24) or **Josh Jung** (50.68). We are closely monitoring the status of **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Miguel Vargas**; as their lineups are currently pending, we have modeled their scores based on assumed slots. A specific risk factor to watch is the wind-in report at **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s venue, which knocked his score down 5% to 58.49 despite his strong underlying xwOBA. We have opted to bench **Brayan Rocchio** (33.90) entirely, as his projected output fell well below our 40-point floor due to a poor spot in the #9 hole and a daunting matchup against Schlittler. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our efficiency metrics in the stolen base category, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 Roto context.",
